==Trivia==
*The stages of this sub-chapter (except for [[Bone Dry Gardens]]) are named after some of Spain's typical foods and drinks, famous places and traditions.
**[[Nyandalucia]] being the Andalucía region, south of Spain.
**[[Paella Field]] is named after [[wikipedia:Paella|a typical food]], most popular in Valencia.
**[[Flamenco Hole]] is named after [[wikipedia:Flamenco|Flamenco]], a music and dance style typical of Andalucía, Murcia and Extremadura.
**[[Sangria River]] refers to [[wikipedia:Sangria|Sangría]], an alcoholic drink made out of wine, fruits and a sweetener.
**[[Gazpacho Highland]]: [[wikipedia:Gazpacho|Gazpacho]] is a cold soup, from Andalucía.
**[[Churros Night]]: Sort of dessert, usually eaten with some hot, sweet, and dense chocolate drink.
**[[Tapas Desert]]: Tapas is the name for the food that usually comes with the drinks you order in a bar.

